<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danes are the North Germanic people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> Danish armies raided and conquered much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and settled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danelaw">Danelaw</a>, and from the 12th century the Danish kingdom expanded into the Baltic, ruling northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> until 1346. Later the Danes held overseas colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a>, and they long ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and the duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and Holstein.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danes.jpg" alt="Danes" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allice Hunter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Danish_Diaspora_in_the_World.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
